The files here were written for these tests, after the vendors' public
documentation of their formats, with example addresses (RFC 5737) and
made-up names and identifiers:

- panos-syslog.log: PAN-OS CONFIG, SYSTEM, GLOBALPROTECT and AUTHENTICATION
  syslog lines in PAN-OS 11.1's field order, an older TRAFFIC line that
  stops early, and a HIPMATCH line (a type read by its common fields only),
  behind RFC 5424 and RFC 3164 headers or none;
- panos-traffic-export.csv, panos-threat-export.csv: CSV exports as the
  web interface writes them, a header row naming the columns;
- fortigate-kv.log: FortiGate key=value lines (traffic forward and local,
  an admin login, SSL-VPN login and tunnel, user authentication, antivirus,
  web filter, IPS and application control), eventtime in seconds,
  milliseconds, microseconds and nanoseconds, or date and time with and
  without tz;
- fortigate-download.csv: FortiGate's CSV log download, one key=value per
  cell, quoted or not;
- asa-syslog.log: Cisco ASA messages the open samples lack (connections
  built outbound and torn down, access group and access list denials, AAA,
  AnyConnect and WebVPN sessions, admin logins and logout, a user added,
  an id this crate doesn't read), with each timestamp form.

